Chapter: DisplayLive
  cites Cvmm chapter DisplayManager
  cites Cvmm chapter CvmmTypes

 The view of the framebuffer the machine was handed. codex-vm writes the GOP
 mode into three handoff cells, the same ones apps/works/DeskVm reads: width
 at 1988, height at 1992, stride at 2016. A zero width means no framebuffer
 was handed over, and the view is empty. GOP reports no refresh rate, so the
 mode's refresh reads 0 rather than a guess.

Section: Handoff Cells

  dl-cell-w : Integer = 1988
  dl-cell-h : Integer = 1992

Section: Mapping

  dm-from-mode : Integer, Integer -> DisplayManagerState
  dm-from-mode (w) (h) =
    if w <= 0 then display-manager-new
    else let gpu = gpu-new "gop0" "UEFI GOP framebuffer" GpuVirtual 0
    in let mode = Resolution { res-width = w, res-height = h, res-refresh = 0 }
    in let mon = display-monitor-new "mon0" "GOP display" ConnVirtual
    in let m1 = __record-set (__record-set (__record-set mon "mon-resolution" mode) "mon-primary" True) "mon-gpu-id" "gop0"
    in disp-add-monitor (disp-add-gpu display-manager-new gpu) m1

  dm-live : DisplayManagerState
  dm-live = dm-from-mode (peek-32 dl-cell-w 0) (peek-32 dl-cell-h 0)

